WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.568
The next morning the travelers passed through the forest and came to a steep hill.

2
00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:12.709
"That will be a difficult climb," said the Scarecrow. "But over it we must go."

3
00:00:12.709 --> 00:00:18.046
He had started up the hill when a rough voice said, "Keep back!"

4
00:00:18.047 --> 00:00:21.514
"Who are you?" asked the Scarecrow.

5
00:00:21.515 --> 00:00:26.809
"This hill belongs to us. You cannot cross it," said the voice again.

6
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:30.359
"But we must cross it," said the Scarecrow.

7
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.478
"You will not!" said a flat-headed, armless creature.

8
00:00:34.479 --> 00:00:40.258
The Scarecrow did not fear such a helpless creature so he continued up the hill.

9
00:00:40.259 --> 00:00:48.627
The creature's head struck the Scarecrow like a hammer, and the Scarecrow went tumbling down the hill.

10
00:00:48.628 --> 00:00:54.541
The Hammer-Head called down, "Climbing the hill won't be as easy as you think."

11
00:00:54.542 --> 00:01:00.611
As Dorothy helped the Scarecrow up, the Tin Man suggested, "Let's call the Winged Monkeys.

12
00:01:00.612 --> 00:01:03.106
You can command them once more."

13
00:01:03.107 --> 00:01:06.068
Everyone thought it was an excellent idea.

14
00:01:06.069 --> 00:01:14.372
Dorothy put on the golden hat, spread her arms, and said, "By my command."

15
00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:19.998
A moment later the King landed, bowed, and said, "What do you command?"

16
00:01:19.999 --> 00:01:25.156
"Take us to the castle of Glinda, the Good Witch of the South," she answered.

17
00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:29.002
"It shall be done," answered the King.

18
00:01:29.003 --> 00:01:35.876
He and his Monkeys picked up the travelers and flew them south.

19
00:01:35.877 --> 00:01:41.663
The King and his followers dropped Dorothy and her friends off in front of Glinda's castle.

20
00:01:41.664 --> 00:01:46.889
Before the gate were three beautiful girls dressed in red.

21
00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:53.228
As Dorothy approached, one of the girls asked, "Why have you come to Glinda's castle?"

22
00:01:53.229 --> 00:01:56.528
"To see the Good Witch," answered Dorothy.

23
00:01:56.529 --> 00:02:01.950
"What is your name? I will find out if she will see you," said the girl.

24
00:02:01.951 --> 00:02:05.601
Dorothy and her friends gave their names, and soon they were admitted.

25
00:02:05.602 --> 00:02:11.436
They were taken to a room in which a beautiful woman sat upon a ruby throne.

26
00:02:11.437 --> 00:02:15.620
"What can I do for you, my child?" asked Glinda.

27
00:02:15.621 --> 00:02:20.695
"My greatest wish is to return to Kansas," answered Dorothy.

28
00:02:20.696 --> 00:02:26.670
"I can tell you how," said Glinda. "But I will need the golden hat."

29
00:02:26.671 --> 00:02:29.916
"You can have it," said Dorothy gladly.

30
